  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core Marketplace momentum continues, but overall demand remains split: steady consumer-facing activity was offset by a sharp pullback in OEM and National advertising, leaving total top-line growth essentially flat. The environment reflects cautious automaker spending even as the platform’s audience and data-driven tools sustain relevance. Profitability improved materially, and cash generation strengthened, pointing to a business that is extracting better economics from a mixed demand backdrop.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership delivered on guidance and exceeded margin expectations while turning prior-year losses into net income. The team signaled confidence by meaningfully raising the share-repurchase target and outlining a multi-year cost-savings program, reinforcing a disciplined capital-allocation stance. The market responded with an analyst upgrade and a higher price target, though some large brokers remain neutral with tempered expectations, suggesting that execution credibility is improving but top-line reinvigoration still needs to be proven.",
